WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.599 --> 00:00:08.360
“So, finally all the straw hats have made
it safely to Wano.”

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.180
“But…”
“About time everyone got reunited after

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:12.949
all that´s happened. “
“Wait…”

00:00:12.949 --> 00:00:16.660
“It just feels really good to have the entire
crew back in one spot. “

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:21.350
“But, Brago, what about Jinbe?”
“Uhm, who the hell is Jinbe?”

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:27.660
“I´m glad you asked!”
I think it goes without saying that Oda is

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:33.000
a great fan of themes and patterns when it
comes to writing his story. No matter if it´s

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.579
the distinct way he builds every single arc
or his affinity for the number 3 Oda clearly

00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:43.829
likes to bring some elements of structure
into his enormous worldbuilding. The example

00:00:43.829 --> 00:00:48.379
that you might be most familiar with though,
is the distinct pattern, based on which he

00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:53.039
has been building the straw-hat crew. Every
straw hat has a tragic backstory that has

00:00:53.039 --> 00:00:58.460
left them emotionally struggling. Every straw
hat has a dream that they can pursue by joining

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:04.070
Luffy. But most importantly, every straw hat
has stuck with Luffy and dedicated his life

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:09.590
to him ever since meeting him.
And that is where Jinbe comes into play. Because

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:14.710
not only has he been the only new crew member
to join after the time skip, but he also hasn´t

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:20.799
traveled with the crew, even a single time.
How is that? Why is Jinbe´s arc so very different

00:01:20.799 --> 00:01:24.750
from the other straw hats, even though he
fulfills pretty much all of the criteria that

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:30.329
constitute a true straw hat? With the introduction
of his character, Oda has deliberately broken

00:01:30.329 --> 00:01:35.399
the pattern for how a new straw hat is supposed
to join the crew. As we will see, there are

00:01:35.399 --> 00:01:41.259
three big reasons for this: The purpose of
the time skip, the complex political structures

00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:47.710
of the New World, but most importantly Jinbe´s
selfless personality. Not only does all this

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:52.510
make him a unique member of the crew, but
also an incredibly intricate character that

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:58.041
keeps impacting the story in quite significant
ways. And if we just take a step back, we

00:01:58.041 --> 00:02:02.799
will see that Jinbe’s character actually
embodies a central moral message that Oda

00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:08.210
tackles within the story. So, let´s take
a closer look at the helmsman of the straw-hat´s

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:11.890
and what role he has to play in the story
of One Piece.

00:02:11.890 --> 00:02:17.270
Oh, and before we get going, as you know Jinbe
is the last official member of the straw hats.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:22.550
So, that would make this video the very last
in this series. But since it seems like you

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:27.160
guys are really enjoying watching these and
I really love making them, I figured we might

00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:32.171
keep this up a bit longer. So, why not make
this a bit of a challenge for all of us? If

00:02:32.171 --> 00:02:37.660
this video gets 2000 likes within the first
24 hours, the next Character Analysis will

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:43.720
be out within a week. A true challenge for
you guys, I think. But especially one for

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.393
me, since I usually take at least twice that
time to make a video like this. Also, pause

00:02:47.393 --> 00:02:53.120
this video for a second, had down to the comment
section and type in the character or group

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:58.930
that YOU think I should do next. The comment
with the most likes gets himself a video,

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:02.880
maybe already next week. So smash that like
button.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:10.430
But now let´s dive right into the world of
our karate-loving fishman.

00:03:10.430 --> 00:03:14.540
When we look at his backstory, we will not
only see that it fulfills the requirements

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:19.810
for being a straw hat, but also gives us the
first clue to why Jinbe can sometimes feel

00:03:19.810 --> 00:03:25.370
a bit out of focus and hard to grasp in the
story. Being the only non-human in the crew,

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:30.730
next to Chopper, who at least ate the human-human
fruit, Jinbe is the first straw hat that brings

00:03:30.730 --> 00:03:36.250
the issue of racial inequality into the crew.
As a result, his past as a fishman is very

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:41.910
different from any of the other straw hats.
Jinbei grew up as an orphan on fishman island

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:47.140
together with Arlong and Fisher Tiger. From
an early age on he practiced fishman-karate,

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:52.980
a powerful martial art, that he managed to
master like no other. When he became older,

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:57.810
he joined the royal military, but left a few
years later, after his friend Fisher Tiger

00:03:57.810 --> 00:04:03.040
invaded Mary-Geoise, and he decided to join
the Sun Pirates instead. Having witnessed

00:04:03.040 --> 00:04:07.291
all of the injustice, that the fishmen had
to suffer by the hand of the humans, young

00:04:07.291 --> 00:04:13.200
Jinbe is rather violent and hateful. We can
see him brutality beating unconscious Marines

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:18.510
accusing them of tolerating slavery and the
discrimination of his people. Slowly however

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:23.150
that sentiment begins to change, as Fisher
Tiger passes his vision for peace between

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:28.260
the races down to Jinbe. He manages to make
him more aware of the endless cycle of hate

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:33.851
and revenge between fishman and humans, that
has to be broken. A few years later, the Sun

00:04:33.851 --> 00:04:40.490
Pirates meet the former human slave-girl Koala.
After taking her in, Jinbe realized how traumatized

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:45.130
she was and starts to build a relationship
with her. He starts to understand that not

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:49.350
all humans are evil and that fishmen aren´t
the only ones to suffer under the reign of

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:54.400
the World Government. When they finally reach
Koala´s village, they are ambushed by the

00:04:54.400 --> 00:05:00.900
Marines and Fisher Tiger is fatally wounded
in the process. After this heavy blow, Jinbe

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:05.820
becomes the new captain of the Sun Pirates.
Despite also having to witness Otohime´s

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:10.590
death by the hands of the Tenryubito later,
Jinbe decides to take on his former captain’s

00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:15.790
dream and try to break the wheel of hate.
He becomes one of the Shijibukai, joining

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:21.850
forces with the world government that he despises
so much, in order to protect his people. However,

00:05:21.850 --> 00:05:27.410
when Whitebeard declares war over Ace´s execution,
Jinbe refuses to answer the government´s

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:32.890
call. After all, White Beard had been protecting
Fishman island under his flag. As a result,

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:38.540
Jinbe is stripped of his rank and thrown into
level 6 of Impel Down. He ends up in the same

00:05:38.540 --> 00:05:43.470
cell as Ace. This is where we first get to
meet him in the story.

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:49.660
So, as you can see, Jinbe clearly fulfills
the criterium of having a tragic backstory.

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:54.280
Not only have the Fishmen been suffering as
a race collectively for many centuries, but

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:59.130
Jinbe also had to witness the consequences
of racial inequality through the deaths of

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:04.971
many people close to him. As we will see,
racism is the great theme of Jinbe´s character

00:06:04.971 --> 00:06:10.271
arc. However, before we can look at how Jinbe
carries that theme throughout the plot, we

00:06:10.271 --> 00:06:18.940
first have to understand the kind of person
he is in general.

00:06:18.940 --> 00:06:24.030
In a way, you could argue that Jinbe is what
Brook might have been to the crew, hadn´t

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:28.910
he been stranded in the Florian Triangle for
50 years of his life. The fishman is a veteran

00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:33.650
pirate, that has a very holistic understanding
of the political and social workings of the

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:38.260
One-Piece world. Since his tragic past as
well as the responsibility for his people

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:43.889
weigh heavily on his shoulders, Jinbe usually
presents himself as a very serious and proud

00:06:43.889 --> 00:06:49.710
warrior. However, if the circumstances allow
for it, he shows us his lighthearted and gentle

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:55.341
side at times. I would argue, that THIS side
comes a lot closer to what Jinbe´s true self

00:06:55.341 --> 00:07:00.630
would really be, if you took away all the
hardship in his life. So, if you ever wondered,

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:05.830
why Jinbe needs the Straw hats in the first
place, this is why. Jinbe can learn to enjoy

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:10.911
life again and can allow himself to drop his
shell when being with the crew. However, he

00:07:10.911 --> 00:07:16.220
also brings a lot to Luffy and the others
in return. First and foremost, having been

00:07:16.220 --> 00:07:21.450
part of the Shijibukai for 11 years, Jinbe
is not only a valuable source of knowledge

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:27.030
and experience, but also brings significant
fighting power to the crew. This is complemented

00:07:27.030 --> 00:07:32.480
by the fact, that he has mastered fishman-karate,
possibly making him one of the strongest fighters

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:38.001
underwater. Apart from battle though, Jinbe
also takes the role of the helmsman. While

00:07:38.001 --> 00:07:43.430
the crew somehow managed so far without one,
Whole Cake Island showed us how valuable it

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:48.240
can be to have this position filled with someone
who knows what they are doing. Beside that

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:53.800
though, being a fishman, Jinbe is also able
to control the sea currents and even talk

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:58.560
to the creatures of the ocean. All of these
skills make him a true upgrade on the Sunny,

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:03.590
that will have to face more and more dangerous
situations in the future.

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:08.650
From an internal perspective, Jinbe´s psychological
need has been constantly shifting over the

00:08:08.650 --> 00:08:13.680
course of the story, which speaks for really
well writing from Oda´s side. It keeps the

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:19.699
story vivid and gives us continuous character
development. In general, Jinbe´s need is

00:08:19.699 --> 00:08:24.889
always focused around his initial hatred towards
the humans for what they did to his people.

00:08:24.889 --> 00:08:29.710
He needs to find a way to break the wheel
of hatred in himself before he can start breaking

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:35.089
the wheel in general. Especially in his younger
years, this moral need also affects those

00:08:35.089 --> 00:08:40.509
around him. We can see this in his violence
against humans, but also in the indifference

00:08:40.509 --> 00:08:46.730
he shows for Otohime´s dream to facilitate
peace. However, as we all know, Jinbe gets

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:51.879
a significant amount of character development
over the course of time. As a result, his

00:08:51.879 --> 00:08:57.860
initial hate towards the humans, slowly but
steadily shifts and finally, Jinbe acquires

00:08:57.860 --> 00:09:04.439
his dream, that is a crucial element of becoming
a straw hat. His dream is to make coexistence,

00:09:04.439 --> 00:09:08.509
equality and friendship between humans and
fish-man possible and put his people out of

00:09:08.509 --> 00:09:12.180
the misery under that they have been suffering
for centuries.

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:17.139
As a result, Jinbe has built a distinct set
of values over the course of his life, that

00:09:17.139 --> 00:09:22.800
fully reflect his change in character. Being
a proud warrior of the sea, Jinbe has a strong

00:09:22.800 --> 00:09:29.279
sense of loyalty and duty. No matter the circumstances,
Jinbe always tries to act honorable and true

00:09:29.279 --> 00:09:34.619
to his word. While he prioritizes the loyalty
towards his people and towards Luffy over

00:09:34.619 --> 00:09:40.540
all else, he tries to avoid going back on
his word as hard as possible. We can see this

00:09:40.540 --> 00:09:45.209
in the relationship with the world government,
to which he stayed faithful until they threatened

00:09:45.209 --> 00:09:50.079
to take down the man who was protecting his
people. Or in his relationship with Big Mom,

00:09:50.079 --> 00:09:54.810
who he tries to compensate fairly, by bringing
her a Poneglyph, before asking to leave her

00:09:54.810 --> 00:10:01.139
crew in order to join Luffy. This also reflects
in Jinbe´s strong believe in taking responsibility

00:10:01.139 --> 00:10:07.970
for your actions. He expects this from others,
but mostly from himself. For example, he begs

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:12.990
Nami for forgiveness for Arlong´s treatment
of her village, feeling responsible for letting

00:10:12.990 --> 00:10:18.300
Arlong go and do as he pleased. Due to his
life-experience Jinbe also sees the importance

00:10:18.300 --> 00:10:23.459
of thoughtfulness in your actions. He always
seems to think things through and then reach

00:10:23.459 --> 00:10:28.769
a conclusion to when and how something should
be done. Did he join Luffy right on Fishman

00:10:28.769 --> 00:10:34.110
Island, which he clearly wanted to do? No,
he waits for the right moment in order to

00:10:34.110 --> 00:10:39.660
not cause any trouble for Luffy OR his people.
And that already brings us to Jinbe´s most

00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:45.300
defining trait, his sense of selflessness.
Like no other character in the story, does

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:51.760
he center his life around that of others.
Jinbe would die for his people or for Luffy.

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:57.220
Their fate is what keeps him going. Whether
it´s protecting Luffy from Akainu by taking

00:10:57.220 --> 00:11:02.819
the hit himself or protecting his people from
exploitation by becoming a pirate and allying

00:11:02.819 --> 00:11:08.069
himself with forces like the world government
or Big Mom. Jinbe truly takes altruism to

00:11:08.069 --> 00:11:12.170
the next level.
All this makes Jinbe a central driver of the

00:11:12.170 --> 00:11:17.350
plot in the story. He saves Luffy multiple
times during the war at Marineford, ensuring

00:11:17.350 --> 00:11:22.050
his survival. And on Whole Cake Island, is
he not only the one to free Luffy and Nami

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:27.110
from Big Mom´s capture, but later also lets
the crew safely escape the grasp of the Yonko

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:31.869
by stirring the Sunny and later staying behind
to hold off their enemies.

00:11:31.869 --> 00:11:36.639
So now that we know, what defines Jinbe as
a character in the story, let´s now look

00:11:36.639 --> 00:11:45.069
at his character arc.
Based on his background and especially the

00:11:45.069 --> 00:11:50.100
intention behind the fishmen-island arc, the
big theme of Jinbe´s character is racial

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:56.110
inequality, discrimination and racism as a
whole. Every aspect of his development arc

00:11:56.110 --> 00:12:01.410
revolves around events that highlight a different
side of the conflict between humans and fishmen.

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:06.329
I don´t want to get too deep into, why the
theme of fishman-island was racism and how

00:12:06.329 --> 00:12:11.540
Oda draws parallels to our society, I think
that would need an entire video on its own.

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:16.699
But I think we can all agree, that with Jinbe,
Oda tries to introduce a character that struggles

00:12:16.699 --> 00:12:20.809
with the way his people are treated by the
rest of the world and at the same time tries

00:12:20.809 --> 00:12:27.040
to work for a better future. Obviously, his
backstory sets the premise for this development.

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:32.119
Being exposed to the cruelty towards his people,
young Jinbe develops a deep hatefulness towards

00:12:32.119 --> 00:12:37.499
the humans. After inheriting Fisher Tigers
will and meeting the former slave girl Koala

00:12:37.499 --> 00:12:42.389
however, Jinbe develops a more refined view
of the humans. And while he still resents

00:12:42.389 --> 00:12:47.779
the way the humans rule the world and suppress
other races, he also understands that this

00:12:47.779 --> 00:12:52.610
is not true for all of them and learns that
other humans have to suffer from their system

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:58.110
as well. As a result, he overcomes his first
moral need and starts dedicating his life

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:03.639
to creating a more positive world for the
fishmen. Now however, we see Jinbe being caught

00:13:03.639 --> 00:13:08.600
in between his resentment and his wish to
make peace with the humans. Working for the

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:12.870
world government violates his ideals and he
emotionally suffers from supporting their

00:13:12.870 --> 00:13:18.300
cause in exchange for his people´s safety.
This is where Marineford comes into play.

00:13:18.300 --> 00:13:22.959
He decides to trust and support White Beard
who has decided to put Fishman-Island under

00:13:22.959 --> 00:13:28.279
his protection. Now, he has actually formed
a connection with humans that value him and

00:13:28.279 --> 00:13:34.019
his people solely for who they are as a person.
And again, he has to see them being crushed

00:13:34.019 --> 00:13:39.160
by the world government. So now, having lost
his strongest lead to a peaceful and friendly

00:13:39.160 --> 00:13:43.790
future through White Beard´s death, Jinbe
now needs to find new hope for his dream.

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:49.250
And that brings us to fishman-island, where
Jinbe truly befriends Luffy, whom he had learned

00:13:49.250 --> 00:13:54.959
to respect during the war. Here he sees someone
who truly doesn´t know or understand the

00:13:54.959 --> 00:13:59.899
concept of racism, but only wants to help
people and sail the sea together with his

00:13:59.899 --> 00:14:05.209
crew. That this crew involves a talking reindeer,
a skeleton and a cyborg, as well as people

00:14:05.209 --> 00:14:09.759
like Nico Robin that have also suffered heavily
from the cruelty of the government are all

00:14:09.759 --> 00:14:16.720
factors that have a big impact on Jinbe. But
probably none as big as meeting Nami. A human,

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:22.259
who now in return has suffered heavily under
the retaliating hate that Arlong brought with

00:14:22.259 --> 00:14:28.111
him towards the humans. Seeing that Nami bears
no ill feelings towards his people, despite

00:14:28.111 --> 00:14:33.449
what happened to her, truly makes Luffy and
the Straw Hats the new source for his hopes.

00:14:33.449 --> 00:14:38.319
All that is left for him now is to fulfill
his dream and also find joy for himself once

00:14:38.319 --> 00:14:43.759
again in his life, that he has solely dedicated
to others. Seeing on Whole Cake Island, how

00:14:43.759 --> 00:14:48.470
Big Mom´s forced idea of a coexistence of
the races doesn´t work, finally being able

00:14:48.470 --> 00:14:53.459
to officially join the straw hats was a big
step in that direction for him. And the great

00:14:53.459 --> 00:14:58.199
thing with Jinbe is, that with this final
need for happiness still not fulfilled, he

00:14:58.199 --> 00:15:02.589
actually has some real character development
left in the story for him to happen, making

00:15:02.589 --> 00:15:08.980
him a very fascinating character.
So, “who the hell is Jinbe”? Jinbe is

00:15:08.980 --> 00:15:14.889
one of the most symbolic and moral-heavy characters
in the entire series. Not only has he shaped

00:15:14.889 --> 00:15:19.809
some of the most significant events in the
current storyline, but he also has been going

00:15:19.809 --> 00:15:25.470
through one of the most complex and long-lasting
character arcs in the story by far. He has

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:30.059
managed to break the wheel of hate between
fishmen and humans and is now striving for

00:15:30.059 --> 00:15:34.800
a better and safer future for his people,
where equal and peaceful coexistence between

00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:40.449
the races is possible. So why did Oda make
an exception with Jinbe and didn´t let him

00:15:40.449 --> 00:15:46.470
join the crew right away? Reason one was the
purpose of the time skip. After the time-skip

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:51.199
it was Oda´s task to show us how each of
the straw hats has grown and how the crew

00:15:51.199 --> 00:15:57.269
of rookies has now become a real pirate crew
that can play with the pros. Secondly, the

00:15:57.269 --> 00:16:01.610
complex political structures of the New World
with all the players involved, would have

00:16:01.610 --> 00:16:07.149
been far less interesting to explore with
someone in the crew who knew about all this.

00:16:07.149 --> 00:16:11.829
But most importantly it was Jinbe´s selfless
personality that led him to prioritize the

00:16:11.829 --> 00:16:17.050
well-being of his people over joining in on
the adventure right away. Keeping his relationship

00:16:17.050 --> 00:16:22.639
with Big Mom was crucial to not spark conflict
for his country. As a result, he hasn´t joined

00:16:22.639 --> 00:16:27.389
up with the crew yet. He doesn´t feel like
a real straw hat yet and still has gotten

00:16:27.389 --> 00:16:32.139
way more character development and action
than some other crew members. I feel like

00:16:32.139 --> 00:16:37.970
that is the main reason many people have difficulties
accepting Jinbe as part of the crew. However,

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:43.720
I will promise you that once he joins up with
the crew that will change. Because not only

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:48.920
does our Whaleshark fulfill all requirements
to be part of the crew, he also brings a lot

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:54.509
more to the story in terms of symbolism and
personality. He is someone living for his

00:16:54.509 --> 00:17:04.799
captain and his people. A truly selfless man.
Hey everybody. Thank you so much for watching.

00:17:04.799 --> 00:17:09.770
I know that this video was a little different
than usual. Nonetheless, I think it shows

00:17:09.770 --> 00:17:14.760
us how much thought Oda puts into many of
the concepts he introduces. What are your

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:18.209
thoughts about Jinbe? Let me know in the comments
below.

